=== 4/4  Asking your agent (main.py ask) ==============================

The income statement shows revenues and expenses using the accrual basis of accounting, meaning it does not indicate how much cash was actually received for revenues or paid for expenses. [accounting-for-managers | 12.1]

The balance sheet shows assets, liabilities, and owners' equity at a specific point in time, but it does not show how much cash was received or paid for these individual items. [accounting-for-managers | 12.1]

The balance sheet and income statement lack detailed cash flow information because they do not disclose cash receipt and cash payment activities over a period of time beyond the net change in cash from the beginning to the end of the period. [accounting-for-managers | 12.1]

The statement of cash flows provides cash receipt and cash payment information, reconciles the change in cash for a period of time, and indicates where cash came from and where cash went by categorizing transactions into operating, investing, or financing activities. [accounting-for-managers | 12.1]

